# INDEX RULES

Indexes are designed from actual workload.

Before adding an index:
1. identify query;
2. identify predicates;
3. identify joins;
4. identify ordering/grouping;
5. inspect existing indexes;
6. evaluate cardinality;
7. estimate write cost;
8. validate with execution plan when material.

NEVER:
- index every column;
- add duplicate indexes;
- create giant hierarchy indexes blindly;
- create indexes solely because a tool suggested them;
- add INCLUDE columns without covering evidence.

Review indexes for:
School, Academic Year, Branch, Class, Section, Student, Teacher assignment, Attendance, Marks, Timetable, Fees and Receipts.

Performance optimization must never weaken correctness or authorization.
